[size=6][b]Bigger Armies — more ground forces for your faction in SpaceBourne 2[/b][/size]

In SpaceBourne 2 your faction's forces are its generals, and each general leads 4 soldiers. A new faction gets 10 general slots, 5 for Ground Forces and 5 for Space Forces: 10 squads, 50 men. "Fifty men isn't exactly an army to conquer the galaxy." Bigger Armies gives your faction more general slots, so you can field twice as many men.

[b]Links:[/b] [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-BiggerArmies]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/17]Nexus Mods[/url] · UE4SS Lua mod · works alone or with the rest of the realism set.
[b]Install the whole realism set in one go:[/b] the [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-Realism]SpaceBourne 2 Realism installer[/url] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/11]Nexus[/url]).

[line]
[size=5][b]Features[/b][/size]

[size=4][b]A bigger army[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]10 more general slots[/b] by default (5 Ground Forces, 5 Space Forces), on top of the game's own. Each slot is room for a general and 4 soldiers: 50 more men, 100 in all.
[*][b]Up to 110 men.[/b] The game stops recruiting at 110 people in total, so the mod never goes above 22 slots (22 squads of 5).
[/list]

[size=4][b]The game's own way[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Real slots.[/b] The slots are added with the same function the station upgrade uses, so they look and work like the game's slots. Fill them as usual: recruit, promote a soldier to general, give them soldiers.
[*][b]Still costs you.[/b] Every recruit costs 200 Faction Power and a daily fee, as in the game.
[*][b]Your faction first.[/b] Nothing happens until you have founded your faction; the slots appear a few seconds after that, or after loading a save.
[/list]

[size=4][b]On by default[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]No key needed: it works as soon as it is installed.
[/list]

[line]
[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]SpaceBourne 2 (Steam).
[*][url=https://github.com/UE4SS-RE/RE-UE4SS/releases/tag/v3.0.1]UE4SS 3.0.1[/url], a free script loader for Unreal Engine games (the realism installer installs it for you).
[/list]

[line]
[size=5][b]Install[/b][/size]

[b]A. SpaceBourne 2 Realism installer (recommended)[/b] Get it on [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/11]Nexus[/url] or [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-Realism/releases/latest]GitHub[/url]. Tick Bigger Armies and any other mods of the set: it installs UE4SS if you don't have it, switches the mods on and keeps them updated.

[b]B. Manual[/b] (Nexus file, or the zip on the [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-BiggerArmies/releases]releases page[/url])
[list=1]
[*]Extract the zip into your game folder (...\SpaceBourne 2, the one with SpaceBourne2.exe). It creates SB2\Binaries\Win64\Mods\BiggerArmies and switches itself on.
[*]No UE4SS yet? Get [url=https://github.com/UE4SS-RE/RE-UE4SS/releases/tag/v3.0.1]RE-UE4SS 3.0.1[/url] and copy dwmapi.dll, UE4SS.dll and UE4SS-settings.ini into SpaceBourne 2\SB2\Binaries\Win64\.
[/list]

[b]Uninstall:[/b] untick Bigger Armies in the installer or delete the BiggerArmies folder. The slots already added stay in your save and keep working; the game just stops getting new ones from the mod.

[line]
[size=5][b]Settings[/b][/size]

Edit Mods\BiggerArmies\scripts\config.lua, then restart the game. Every line is optional.

[list]
[*]Enabled: false switches the mod off.
[*]ExtraGeneralSlots (10): general slots added on top of the game's own, 0–12. They come in pairs, one Ground Forces and one Space Forces general (the game adds them that way), so an odd number is rounded down. Each slot is room for 5 men.
[/list]

[line]
[size=5][b]Known limits[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]4 soldiers per general[/b] stays as in the game: the faction screen has exactly 4 soldier places per general, and the mod cannot change that screen.
[*][b]Lowering the setting[/b] does not remove slots you already have; the mod only adds.
[*][b]Battles with many squads[/b] put more soldiers on the field, which costs frames on slower PCs. That is the game's own cost; send fewer squads if a big battle runs slowly.
[/list]

[line]
[size=5][b]How it works[/b][/size]

The game keeps your general slots in your faction's data and adds one with its own function when you upgrade your station. A few seconds after a load, the mod counts your slots, works out how many the game itself gave you, and calls that same function until you have the extra ones. It never removes anything. Details: [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-BiggerArmies/blob/main/DESIGN.md]DESIGN.md[/url]. Version history: [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-BiggerArmies/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md]CHANGELOG.md[/url].

[line]
[size=5][b]The SpaceBourne 2 realism set[/b][/size]

Separate mods that work alone or in any combination. The [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-Realism]SpaceBourne 2 Realism installer[/url] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/11]Nexus[/url]) installs the ones you tick and keeps them updated.

[list]
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-HardcoreTacticalRealism]Hardcore Tactical Realism[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/4]Nexus[/url]): realistic ballistics, wounds and tactical AI. The core of the set.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-SilentOps]Silent Ops[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/6]Nexus[/url]): stealth, silent takedowns and suppressors.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-AmmoDiscipline]Ammo Discipline[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/12]Nexus[/url]): carried ammo limits and scavenging, so every magazine counts.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-GearWithoutLevels]Gear Without Levels[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/7]Nexus[/url]): use gear above your level, with small handling penalties.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-TacticalFirstPerson]Tactical First Person[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/15]Nexus[/url]): first person on foot, weapons held up, aiming down the sights.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-TacticalEngineering]Tactical Engineering[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/10]Nexus[/url]): realistic deployable turrets.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-GetOutOfTheWay]Get Out of the Way[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/14]Nexus[/url]): NPCs step aside naturally when you walk through them.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-GroundWaypoints]Ground Waypoints[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/13]Nexus[/url]): planet waypoints on foot and on the hoverbike.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-FactionPower]Faction Power[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/9]Nexus[/url]): dungeons, strategic sales and missions earn your faction power.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-BiggerArmies]Bigger Armies[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/17]Nexus[/url]): twice the general slots for your faction's ground and space forces.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-ClearHUD]Clear HUD[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/16]Nexus[/url]): a reticle you can see and HUD colours of your choice.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-SplitControls]Split Controls[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/5]Nexus[/url]): separate vertical invert for ship and on foot, per device.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-HOTAS]SB2 HOTAS[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/8]Nexus[/url]): HOTAS, rudder pedals, triple screens and head tracking.
[/list]

